psikyosh, deco32, suprnova: speed hacks on by default

The "Speed Hacks" DIP switch turns on idle skipping: when the main CPU
spins in its wait-for-the-next-frame loop, the emulator jumps to the
next interrupt instead. It is off by default, so on a slow CPU these
games run at a fraction of full speed (Gunbird 2 on a Cortex-A35, uncapped:
40 fps off, 160 on). On by default for the lists of Gunbird 2, Strikers
1945 II and III (and Gunbarich), Tetris TGM2, Captain America and The
Avengers, Night Slashers, Cyvern and Puzzle Loop. Saved core options
still override it.

